  "TUB": {
   "geometry_notes": [
    "Web slope 7 vertical : 1 horizontal (drawn slope triangle); 7\" (TYP.) thickness arrow is square to the sloping web, so horizontal thickness = 7*sqrt(50)/7 = 7.0711 in.",
    "Fillets: 1'-0\" (TYP.) vertical from soffit to the web/fillet junction; horizontal run 1'-0\" (G4, G5) or 1'-6\" (G6) as drawn; 6\" bottom slab.",
    "UF flange: 3\" inner overhang from the inner web face and 5\" outer overhang from the outer web face, both at the web junction 6 in below the top; 4 1/2\" square edges; 1 1/2\" taper. Printed block width 1'-3 1/16\" = 15.0625 in is the 1/16-rounded 15.0711 in implied by the overhangs; the overhang convention reproduces all properties exactly, the printed width would not (-0.1 in2).",
    "G6 discrepancy (2006 table only; G6 dropped by 2025): the drawn 1'-6\" fillet run gives areas 36.0 in2 below the table for all six G6 sizes. Re-diagnosis: a 2'-0\" run reproduces the 2006 table A, Yb and Ix exactly for all six (e.g. U54G6 1254.82/18.164/341728 vs 1254.8/18.16/341728). Measured on the 200 dpi render the drawn run scales to ~18 in, so the 2006 drawing and table disagree. Tub detail sheet 5.6-A16-1 (PDF p546) breaks the fillet in its typical section and does not resolve it. The drawn 1'-6\" is implemented (provenance transcribed-with-convention) and the -36 in2 residual pinned in tests.",
    "Iy is checked against the 2025 table for all G4/G5 sizes."
   ],
