  "BTG": {
   "geometry_notes": [
    "W*BTG: 4'-1\" top flange; 3\"/3\"/2\" stack at the web; 1'-6 1/2\" taper run and 3\" bevel run (so 3 + 3 + 18.5 = 24.5 in half width); 6\" web; 2'-1\" bottom flange with 6\" edge and 3\" taper over 9 1/2\". The 1\" bottom chamfer is not labelled on 5.6-A1-3 but is labelled '1\" CHAMFER (TYP.)' on detail 5.6-A13-1 Section C.",
    "Residual vs 2006 Table 5.6.1-1 (the only published set): drawn outline is +4.0 in2 (+0.74 to +0.56%), Yb +0.10 to +0.20 in, Iz +0.06 to +0.37%. The 2006 table omits bottom chamfers elsewhere; without chamfers the excess is 5.0 in2, located (by first-moment balance) about 6 in below the top, i.e. at the flange-taper/bevel junction. No simple reading of the callouts explains it (tested: 2.5/2.75 in edge, narrower flange, no bevel, top chamfers). Drawn geometry kept; residual pinned.",
    "WF*BTG (5.6-A1-4): same depth stack as W*BTG; flange width variable 4'-0\" MIN to 8'-0\" MAX (default 72 in used here). Horizontal taper/bevel runs are not dimensioned on this sheet: assumed equal to W*BTG (18.5 + 3 in), a constant 3 in flat extension beyond (scaled drawing ~19-20 in taper run, consistent). No published properties. Provenance estimate."
   ],
