  "DG": {
   "geometry_notes": [
    "Stack at the web: 6\" flange, 3\" taper, 2\" bevel (2\" horizontal); taper run 1'-7 1/2\" from bevel start; web 6\"; 2'-1\" bottom flange, 6\" edge, 3\" taper over 9 1/2\"; 1\" chamfer.",
    "Flange width: sheet dimension '4'-0\" MIN. - 6'-0\" MAX.' runs to the joint centreline; concrete edge is 1/2\" (TYP.) from the joint at the top and 3/16\" (TYP.) at the bottom lip, so concrete top width = spacing - 1 in. The 2026 PRELIMINARY sheet gives 4'-1\" MIN.",
    "At 48 in spacing the 19.5 in taper would pass the flange tip (3 + 2 + 19.5 = 24.5 > 23.81 in); the taper is clipped at the tip (the 'VARIES' flat is zero). Convention.",
    "Keyway (5.6-A24-2 Section A): 1\" vertical face at top, V recess 2\" deep with apex 3 in below top, returning to the bottom lip at 5 in below top; lower lip at 3/16\" from joint. The lower sloping face end point (lip edge vs upper face line) is a drawing-read convention.",
    "Small half-round drip notch on the flange underside near the tip (drawn, undimensioned) is omitted.",
    "W35DG at 48 in vs Appendix 5-B8 worked example (A 669, yb 20.9, I 100096, Ip 169341 so Iy 69245): A -0.57%, yb +0.25%, I -0.52%, Iy -3.4%. Without the keyway the residuals are +0.43%, +0.8%, +0.34%, +1.6%. Keyway kept because it is drawn and dimensioned. The worked example's own geometry is not given."
   ],
